<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seth</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seth was an ancient Egyptian god of storms, the desert, foreign lands and disorder. In myth he murdered his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osiris">Osiris</a> and fought Osiris's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horus">Horus</a> for the throne, but he also defended the sun god against the serpent Apophis. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hyksos">Hyksos</a> rulers honoured him at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avaris">Avaris</a>, and the Ramesside kings, among them Seti I, took their names from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seth.jpg" alt="Seth" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Feofan Grek · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spas_na_Ilyine_-_Patriarch_Seth_2_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
